WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.950
This is “Every State in the US” by Wendover
Productions and made possible by The Great

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:05.950
Courses Plus.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.769
We’ll start with Alabama, the first state
alphabetically.

00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:13.910
Magnolia Springs, Alabama is the only town
in America to have their mail delivered by

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:18.770
boat, although the longest mail delivery route
in America is in rural Oklahoma where delivery

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:25.599
drivers have to drive 187.6 miles each day
to delivery the mail to around 200 houses.

00:00:25.599 --> 00:00:29.720
Oklahoma’s state vegetable is the watermelon,
which happens to be a fruit, and Oklahoma

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.070
is also home to Kansas, the town.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:37.160
The real Kansas, or more specifically this
point, is the geographic center of the contiguous

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.600
United States.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.239
What Kansas is not home to is Kansas City
which counterintuitively is in Missouri where

00:00:43.239 --> 00:00:47.969
the population center of the US is—the average
location of every American.

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:52.250
Missouri borders eight states, and is therefore
tied with Tennessee as the state that borders

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.100
the most other states.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:58.129
Tennessee was a southern state that seceded
from the United States and joined the confederacy

00:00:58.129 --> 00:01:00.750
in the lead up to the Civil War except for
Scott County which seceded from Tennessee

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.469
and formed an unrecognized independent state.

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:07.940
Scott County didn’t actually officially
rejoin Tennessee until 1986.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:12.590
Tennessee’s western border was originally
defined by the course of the Mississippi River

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:16.510
which has since changed course which has led
to all these enclaves and exclaves of the

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.570
two states on the two sides of the river.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:24.160
The Arkansas River, a major tributary of the
Mississippi, begins all the way in Colorado,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.740
where nobody’s entirely sure which mountain
is the tallest, Mount Elbert or Mount Massive,

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.990
since their heights are within 10 feet of
each other and people keep building piles

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:35.270
of rocks on the summits to make one mountain
taller than the other.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:40.320
Colorado is also home to the America’s longest
continuous street —Colfax Avenue in Denver

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.690
at 26 miles long, but the shortest individually
named street in America is reportedly McKinley

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:50.130
street in Bellefontiane Ohio at a mere 28
feet long.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:54.550
Ohio’s northernmost point is actually south
of Canada’s southernmost point—Pelee island.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:02:00.980
Pelee island, Canada, in fact, is farther
south than parts of 27 states including California

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.650
which as a state has a higher population than
the entire country of Canada.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:11.260
Los Angeles, California, despite being on
the Pacific ocean, is east of six state capitals

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.840
including Reno, Nevada.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:18.120
Nevada has the point in the entire United
States where you’re farthest from a McDonalds—only

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:22.570
116 miles—although Nevada is not the state
with the fewest McDonalds.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:27.040
That title goes to the state with 29 McDonalds,
North Dakota, which according to some legal

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.260
experts wasn’t technically a state until
2012 since their constitution was missing

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:36.780
this sentence which meant it didn’t fulfill
the federal requirements for statehood.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:41.350
Despite having the fewest McDonalds, North
Dakota is not America’s least populated

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:42.350
state.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:46.050
That’s Wyoming which has two sets of escalators
in the entire state.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:50.120
Wyoming is well known for hosting Yellowstone
National Park, although a bit of it spills

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.750
over into Idaho, though in this section you
can get away with murder.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:58.040
You see, with the sixth amendment, if you’re
placed on trial its required that you are

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.290
judged by a jury of your peers which means
individuals from the same state and federal

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:04.570
district as where the crime was committed.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:08.870
Yellowstone is its own Federal district meaning
you’d need residents from Yellowstone to

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:12.710
be on the jury although if you were in the
Idaho part you’d need Yellowstone residents

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:17.350
from Idaho to be on the Jury… except this
50 square mile section is entirely uninhabited,

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:20.940
so they wouldn’t be able to form a jury
which means you’d walk free.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.770
There’s also one single road connecting
the entire southern section of Idaho to the

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.770
northern section.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:31.540
Idaho, with its fairly low population, has
one single telephone area code for the whole

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.910
state, just like neighboring Montana.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:39.300
Montana is home to the least busy commercial
airport in the US—Dawson Community Airport—at

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.069
4,000 passengers per year or about 11 per
day.

00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:48.330
Missoula Montana is also home to the warehouse
of DFTBA where you can buy one of these—a

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.960
Wendover Productions t-shirt—for only $20.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.220
The link is in the description.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:59.760
The busiest airport in America is Atlanta’s
at 49 million passengers per year or 135,000

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.760
per day.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:06.050
Peachtree, a suburb of Atlanta, is a community
that has 90 miles of golf-cart specific roads

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:12.520
adjacent to its normal roads since 9,000 families
here have golf carts as their second cars.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.840
Kids are even encouraged to drive to school
from the age of 12 in their golf carts.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:22.800
Georgia, or more specifically Springer Mountain,
Georgia is the start of the 2,200 mile long

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.540
Appalachian Trail which is a hiking trail
that terminates way up at Mount Katahdin,

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.540
Maine.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.330
Maine is the only state in the United States
to only border one other state and its also

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.740
the closest state to Africa—seriously, its
closer than Florida.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:41.930
The second closest state to Africa is Massachusetts
or more specifically Cape Cod, Massachusetts

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:47.000
which is technically an island since a man-made
canal separates it from the mainland.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:52.000
Massachusetts is actually farther from Miami
than Panama City is, and Miami is closer to

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.980
the country capitals of Nassau Bahamas and
Havana Cuba than to its own state capital—Tallahassee.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:04.210
Florida has the lowest highest point of any
state—312 feet—23 times lower than South

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:05.870
Dakota’s highest point.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:10.660
South Dakota is home to the geographic center
of the entire United States including Alaska

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:15.090
and Hawaii and it was made a state a mere
nine days before Washington, which was called

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:17.300
Columbia before it became a state.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:21.270
Its name was changed as to not confuse it
with the District of Columbia but obviously

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:25.580
that didn’t work out since DC’s city ended
up also being called Washington.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:30.090
Washington Place is the official residence
of Hawaii’s governor and Hawaii was given

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:35.550
its own unique currency during WWII that was
its only legal tender so that, in case the

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:39.950
Japanese successfully invaded Hawaii, the
federal government could declare all of Hawaii’s

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:43.090
currency worthless to prevent the Japanese
from using it.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:48.650
The closest state to Hawaii is Alaska whose
capital, Juneau, has no roads connecting it

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:53.540
with the rest of Alaska or North America meaning
you can’t drive in or out.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:58.120
Alaska is also one of the four states that
completely bans outdoor billboards along with

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:02.830
Hawaii, Maine, and Vermont whose tallest building
is only 11 stories tall.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:05.500
That’s the shortest tallest building of
any state.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.389
The tallest building in the states is Freedom
Tower in New York.

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:11.320
New York is home to Ellis Island, or at least
this part of it.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:15.740
Their territory is completely surrounded by
New Jersey, similar to Liberty Island—home

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.139
to the Statue of Liberty—which is completely
surrounded by New Jersey Waters which means

00:06:20.139 --> 00:06:24.210
you need to travel through New Jersey to get
from New York to New York.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:28.880
Clinton Road in West Milford, New Jersey has
America’s longest red light—a full five

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:29.960
minute wait.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:33.530
New Jersey actually goes surprisingly far
south[(still view of Kentucky’s —farther

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.810
south than Kentucky’s northernmost point.]

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:40.210
In its south-west corner, Kentucky has a rather
large piece of territory thats not actually

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.460
connected to the rest of Kentucky.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:46.090
Kentucky was the birthplace of Lincoln who
was later elected to the Illinois House of

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:50.930
Representatives and in Illinois is the original
burger king, but its not the burger king you’re

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:51.970
thinking of.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:56.410
This burger king existed before this burger
king and therefore sued burger king when they

00:06:56.410 --> 00:07:00.880
came to Illinois for trademark infringement
and won, so now no burger king is allowed

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:04.970
to operate within a 20 mile radius of this
original burger king.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:10.270
Chicago, Illinois, America’s 3rd largest
city, is just a tad larger than the forth

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:15.900
largest city—Houston, Texas and Texas is
so enormous that El Paso, Texas is closer

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:18.860
to Los Angeles than it is to Houston, Texas.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:22.780
Texas’ northernmost point is also closer
to Michigan than it is to its southernmost

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:23.780
point.

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:28.419
From Detroit, Michigan, you actually end up
in Canada if you travel due south and Michigan

00:07:28.419 --> 00:07:32.750
is also the only state to be made of two entirely
separated sections.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:38.199
Michigan’s Highway 185 is actually a bike
path making it the only official highway in

00:07:38.199 --> 00:07:40.500
America where cars are banned.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:45.490
Michigan’s upper peninsula is only connected
by land to Wisconsin which is home to the

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:50.509
Green Bay Packers—a team so popular that
the waiting list for season tickets is 30

00:07:50.509 --> 00:07:51.509
years long.

00:07:51.509 --> 00:07:55.400
It’s so long that its common for parents
to put their kids name on the list as soon

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.410
as they’re born.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:08:01.850
In Watertown, Wisconsin is Utah street, but
the real Utah has the longest section of Interstate

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:06.290
in the US with no gas stations—106 miles
on I-70.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:13.100
I-70 ends over 2,000 miles away in Baltimore,
Maryland and the entire state of Maryland

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.100
has zero natural lakes.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:20.020
It also has this panhandle that reaches a
minimum width of 1.8 miles before expanding

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:25.180
back out to 30 miles width out near West Virginia
which is definitively a southern state but

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:30.320
also has a panhandle that reaches as far north
as New York City and Nebraska.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:35.329
Monowi, Nebraska is the only incorporated
municipality in the United States that have

00:08:35.329 --> 00:08:37.219
a population of one.

00:08:37.219 --> 00:08:42.349
The one resident, Elsie Eiler, is mayor and
runs the library and tavern which is granted

00:08:42.349 --> 00:08:45.540
a liquor license each year by Elsie herself.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:50.429
Tortilla Flat, Arizona is six times larger
than Monowi since it has six residents and

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:56.779
Arizona also has 1/4 of the four corners monument—the
only point where four states meet in the US—Arizona,

00:08:56.779 --> 00:09:02.949
Utah, Colorado, and New Mexico which as a
state, by law, still recognizes Pluto as a

00:09:02.949 --> 00:09:03.949
planet.

00:09:03.949 --> 00:09:08.179
New Mexico is typically the last state to
vote in presidential primaries whereas Iowa

00:09:08.179 --> 00:09:09.589
is usually the first.

00:09:09.589 --> 00:09:15.400
Iowa is the only state in the US whose eastern
and western borders are both water—in this

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.420
case rivers.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:21.430
The eastern border is the Mississippi river,
which happens to be the namesake for Mississippi.

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:27.869
The Mississippi river also flowed backwards
for a full 24 hours in 2012 during Hurricane

00:09:27.869 --> 00:09:32.000
Isaac but the Mississippi doesn’t actually
reach the ocean in Mississippi.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:37.470
It does so in Louisiana—home to the longest
bridge over water in the world at 24 miles.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:43.000
That’s so long that for eight of those miles,
you can’t even see land on either side.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.910
One of the other longest bridges in the US
is in North Carolina—the the Virginia Dare

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:51.439
Memorial Bridge which carries cars out to
Kitty Hawk where the Wright Brothers successfully

00:09:51.439 --> 00:09:55.100
flew a heavier than air aircraft for the first
time in history.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:10:02.079
It was a 12 second, 120 foot flight—thats
shorter than the wingspan of a Boeing 747.

00:10:02.079 --> 00:10:06.129
North Carolina’s southern neighbor is South
Carolina although South Carolina isn’t all

00:10:06.129 --> 00:10:10.649
that south since more than half of it is north
of North Carolina’s southernmost point and

00:10:10.649 --> 00:10:15.410
South Carolina also has a town called North
making it North, South Carolina.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:19.420
South Carolina was the site of the first civil
war battle and the civil war ended up having

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:25.230
a total of one battle over in Indiana where
the Indy 500 speedway is which is so enormous

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:29.240
that you could comfortably fit the entire
country of the vatican inside it.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:35.509
It can also fit 400,000 people which is the
highest capacity of any sports arena in the

00:10:35.509 --> 00:10:36.509
world.

00:10:36.509 --> 00:10:39.730
Indiana’s state beverage is water, while
Oregon’s is milk.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:44.240
Portland, Oregon is home to the world’s
smallest park according to the Guinness world

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.319
records book—mill end park.

00:10:46.319 --> 00:10:50.899
Oregon is also one of the few states to not
have a sales tax along with New Hampshire—the

00:10:50.899 --> 00:10:54.690
only state to have no law requiring adults
to wear seat belts.

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:58.160
Connecticut Lake, in New Hampshire, is the
source of the Connecticut River which is what

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:00.320
Connecticut the state is named after.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:05.029
Hartford, Connecticut's airport, at less than
3 million passengers per year, is the smallest

00:11:05.029 --> 00:11:08.089
airport in the US to have a direct flight
to Europe.

00:11:08.089 --> 00:11:12.420
Delaware, on the other hand, certainly doesn’t
have a direct flight to Europe since its the

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:14.310
only state that you can’t fly to.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:18.089
There’s not one commercial flight in or
out of this tiny state.

00:11:18.089 --> 00:11:23.059
It’s the second smallest state behind Rhode
Island which is so small that the entire state

00:11:23.059 --> 00:11:25.730
grows by 3% during low tide.

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:29.959
Rhode Island’s second largest city, Warwick,
shares its name with Warwick Pennsylvania

00:11:29.959 --> 00:11:35.699
and in Pennsylvania is Centralia where the
ground has been on fire since 1962 due to

00:11:35.699 --> 00:11:41.160
a coal mine fire and its expected to burn
for over 200 years.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:46.189
Pennsylvania borders Minnesota, well not really,
but Pennsylvania Avenue does intersect Minnesota

00:11:46.189 --> 00:11:50.619
Avenue in DC, and Minnesota is home to the
northernmost point in the lower 48.

00:11:50.619 --> 00:11:56.079
You see, most of the US-Canada border is defined
by the 49th parallel but a surveying error

00:11:56.079 --> 00:11:57.220
led to this.

00:11:57.220 --> 00:12:01.220
The couple hundred residents of this area,
called the Northwest angle, are completely

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:05.899
cut off from the US and need to pass into
Canada then back into the United states to

00:12:05.899 --> 00:12:07.120
go to school.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:12.170
Also in northern Minnesota is Virginia, the
town, but Virginia, the state is massive.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:16.720
So massive that Ewing, Virigina, is closer
to eight other state capitals than it is to

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:18.759
its own state capital, Richmond.

00:12:18.759 --> 00:12:23.949
Alexandria, Virginia is actually closer to
Toronto, Canada than it is to Ewing, Virginia.

00:12:23.949 --> 00:12:27.309
Virginia also happens to go farther west than
west Virginia.

00:12:27.309 --> 00:12:32.069
Virginia is also home to this place, the headquarters
of the Teaching Company who run the Great

00:12:32.069 --> 00:12:33.269
Courses Plus.

